sonar_slam_frontend — front end of the Ping360 sonar SLAM system (BSD-3-Clause)

Provenance
----------
src/stateEstimation/  and  src/generalHelpfulTools/  are derived from
constructor-robotics/underwaterSLAM_2D_lowCost (ROS 2 package
"low_cost_underwater_slam", maintainer Tim Hansen, Constructor University
Bremen; its package.xml declares the BSD license), the open-source stack of

  T. Hansen and A. Birk, "An Open-Source Solution for Fast and Accurate
  Underwater Mapping with a Low-Cost Mechanical Scanning Sonar,"
  Proc. IEEE ICRA, 2024.

The derived EKF provides the DVL/IMU odometry used by Ping-SLAM.

Modifications (2026), see the "Modified" comments at the top of each file
for the full list:
  src/stateEstimation/ekfDVL.cpp, ekfDVL.h
    - three-axis IMU mount rotation (rollMountIMU/pitchMountIMU/yawMountIMU)
      applied inside the filter, so vertical / inverted IMUs are supported
  src/stateEstimation/ekfDVLnode.cpp
    - three-axis DVL mount rotation (replaces the single yawRotationDVL)
    - constant gyro-bias subtraction (gyroBiasX/Y/Z) before fusion
    - DVL reports flagged invalid are skipped instead of zero-filled
  src/generalHelpfulTools/
    - retained Eigen/tf2 helpers use a modified build layout
    - unused PeakFinder code is not distributed in this package

Written for this project (not derived from upstream):
  src/sonarToLaserscan/sonarToLaserscan.cpp   pseudo-scan builder
  src/tools/rosGtSaver.cpp                     mocap ground-truth dump
  scripts/analyze_scan_bag.py
